#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:9
msgid "Virtual Switch Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:11
msgid ""
"A Virtual Switch is a cluster-level networking abstraction that "
"simplifies host network configuration across layout 2.0 HVM compute "
"nodes. Rather than manually configuring bridges, bonds, and VLANs on each"
" host via CLI, Virtual Switches allow administrators to define network "
"intent once and have it applied consistently across the entire cluster."
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:13
msgid "Virtual Switches manage:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:15
msgid "**Uplink selection** — Which physical NICs carry traffic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:16
msgid "**Bond creation** — Aggregating multiple NICs for redundancy or throughput"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:17
msgid "**Traffic separation** — Isolating VM, storage, migration, and SDN traffic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:18
msgid "**VLAN handling** — Tagging traffic for network segmentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:19
msgid ""
"**IP addressing** — Assigning host-level IPs for storage and migration "
"networks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hvm/virtual_switches.rst:21
msgid ""
"Each layout 2.0 HVM cluster supports up to **8 Virtual Switches**. A "
"default Virtual Switch named ``vs0`` is created automatically during "
"cluster provisioning and handles VM network traffic."
msgstr ""

